e-registered reading fired once on 2026-10-07 and never re-run, re-ordered or re-thresholded, 240 of 240 generations parsed, n = 10 per shape; the grader is the dev probe's `identifies` label over the first hypothesis statement only (the cue's `scope_id` as a whole word, neither neighbour in `[a-z0-9_-]`, AND a retry token; negation is not read, a space-separated sibling passes, `retried` is not a token); the bar is `both` ≥ 36/40 over the ordinary shapes S1–S4 and ≥ 19/20 over the sibling shapes S7 + S8 (a retry storm scoped to `conductor` beside a `conductor-canary` services row, S8 with two corpus lines naming the canary). It read `shipped` 40/40 · 20/20, the v2.5 baseline `ns` 38/40 · 20/20, and the harness-only line-bearing renders `L` and `LI` 40/40 · 20/20 each: every arm met the bar, the selection is `shipped`, the verdict PASS, and the regression guard (the sentence is reverted if `shipped` reads below `ns` on either half) HOLDS. What the reading does not show stands beside it: the baseline arm met the bar too, so the probe had no known-positive for the miss Conductor's fourth series hit (the storm attributed to the hyphenated sibling in 1 of 3 end-to-end drives); the sentence's measured effect is two generations on one ordinary shape (S3), and whether it fixes that case was unmeasured at that chunk; the next chunk measured it on replayed product prompts, where `shipped`, which carries the sentence, read 9 of 20 `both` on one prompt of three — the sentence alone does not fix it. **The canary-history readings and the corpus-selection remedy** (chunk 2026-10-07-l4-probe-reproduces-the-canary-history-miss; as measured at its `evidence/reading-reproduction.md`, `reading-replay.md`, `reading-remedy.md` and `reading-third.md`; the shipped gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_K_M through llama-cli b9305, the same `identifies` grader, each reading pre-registered and run once on 2026-10-07). *Synthetic shapes:* `shipped` over S7–S16, n = 20 a shape, read 199 of 200 `both` (one `signal